        "original_id": "846ebc6b-26d0-529f-bb4c-d5441ed63d78",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Carol Lawrence, Paul Lynde, Alice Ghostley, Eartha Kitt, Robert Clary, Ronny Graham, Mel Brooks, Sheldon Harnick\n- Works: New Faces of 1952\n- Roles: actress, performer, writer, lyricist\n- Topics: musical theatre, television\n\nFacts:\n- New Faces of 1952 helped jump-start the careers of Paul Lynde, Alice Ghostley, Eartha Kitt, Robert Clary, Carol Lawrence, Ronny Graham, Mel Brooks, and Sheldon Harnick.\n- In New Faces of 1952, Mel Brooks was credited as Melvin Brooks.\n- In New Faces of 1952, Sheldon Harnick was a lyricist.\n- Carol Lawrence was born on September 5, 1932.\n- Carol Lawrence is an American actress most often associated with musical theatre.\n- Carol Lawrence has also appeared extensively on television.",
